WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.509 --> 00:00:03.195
- [Voiceover] Just 45 minutes
north of the U.S. border

00:00:03.195 --> 00:00:04.984
is a city called Langley.

00:00:04.984 --> 00:00:06.485
It's a typical city.

00:00:06.485 --> 00:00:09.220
There is a casino, tree-lined streets,

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:11.883
and, of course, a Ghanaian tribal chief.

00:00:11.883 --> 00:00:14.966
(light upbeat music)

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:18.028
This is Eric Manu.

00:00:18.028 --> 00:00:19.903
He works in Langley as a gardener

00:00:19.903 --> 00:00:22.320
for this woman, Susan Watson.

00:00:23.287 --> 00:00:26.013
In Canada, yard work is
a year-round occupation.

00:00:26.013 --> 00:00:30.180
- You'd be surprised how busy
we are during the winter.

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:33.311
- [Voiceover] Back to Eric.

00:00:33.311 --> 00:00:36.285
Eric's story began with
a phone call last July.

00:00:36.285 --> 00:00:37.824
- Yeah, my uncle died,

00:00:37.824 --> 00:00:41.515
and I got a call to take
over that responsibility

00:00:41.515 --> 00:00:44.107
as a chief of my community,

00:00:44.107 --> 00:00:46.486
and that's in Aboabo Number 2.

00:00:46.486 --> 00:00:47.770
- [Voiceover] He said something like:

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:48.604
- Really?

00:00:48.604 --> 00:00:50.596
Are you kidding me?

00:00:50.596 --> 00:00:52.294
I said, "I'm gonna give it a try."

00:00:52.294 --> 00:00:55.209
- [Voiceover] So he went back
to Ghana and became chief,

00:00:55.209 --> 00:00:57.473
but he decided to return to Langley,

00:00:57.473 --> 00:00:59.946
and this is when Susan got involved,

00:00:59.946 --> 00:01:02.284
and where our contemporary story begins.

00:01:02.284 --> 00:01:05.135
Everything that happened
after Eric became chief.

00:01:05.135 --> 00:01:07.164
- [Eric] I have seen so much in Canada.

00:01:07.164 --> 00:01:10.953
That's my own experience,
and I also want my people

00:01:10.953 --> 00:01:14.811
to have some kind of opportunity in life.

00:01:14.811 --> 00:01:16.483
- [Voiceover] With Susan, Eric is working

00:01:16.483 --> 00:01:18.787
on raising funds and collecting donations

00:01:18.787 --> 00:01:20.950
to help set up medical
clinics for his tribe

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:22.803
to improve education.

00:01:22.803 --> 00:01:24.927
Overall, he's trying to make life better

00:01:24.927 --> 00:01:26.975
for his people back home.

00:01:26.975 --> 00:01:29.875
- We started the To the
Moon and Back Foundation

00:01:29.875 --> 00:01:32.576
to help the people in Ghana.

00:01:32.576 --> 00:01:35.547
We've collected more than
two 20-foot containers

00:01:35.547 --> 00:01:37.218
full of donated items.

00:01:37.218 --> 00:01:41.251
- My journey has been a
very successful journey.

00:01:41.251 --> 00:01:43.093
Although I'm a chief in Ghana,

00:01:43.093 --> 00:01:45.659
I'm proud working as a gardener

00:01:45.659 --> 00:01:49.367
to support and give my
people their exposure.

00:01:49.367 --> 00:01:50.914
I'm proud of my community;

00:01:50.914 --> 00:01:52.237
I'm proud of my family;

00:01:52.237 --> 00:01:53.979
and I'm proud to be an African.

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:55.847
And, I'm proud to be a Ghanaian.

00:01:55.847 --> 00:01:58.430
(upbeat music)

